# bat configuration — one CLI argument per line.
#
# Catppuccin is not built into bat, so the theme is vendored as
# themes/catppuccin-mocha.tmTheme — copied verbatim from catppuccin/bat, no
# hand-porting. bat only picks a theme file up from a compiled cache, so after
# a fresh `./install.sh bat` (or any edit to it) run:
#
#     bat cache --build
#
# `bat --list-themes` should then show `catppuccin-mocha`. Note bat names a
# *user* theme after its filename, not the `name` key inside the plist (which
# here is "Catppuccin Mocha"), and a wrong value is silent — bat falls back to
# its built-in Monokai default and prints orange rather than erroring. Verify
# after any rename.
#
# Palette: see docs/palette.md.

--theme="catppuccin-mocha"

# Line numbers, git modification markers and a header per file, but no grid.
--style="numbers,changes,header"

# Only page when the output doesn't fit; keep colors and let bat's default
# less flags through.
--paging=auto
